<h2>How much does a private sunrise boat ride in Varanasi cost?</h2>
<p>Our <a href="/tours/varanasi-boat-ride/">private sunrise boat ride in Varanasi</a> starts from <strong>₹3,250 per person</strong>, based on two guests. The starting total for two guests is therefore <strong>₹6,500, including GST</strong>.</p>
<p>This includes a private motorboat and an English-speaking guide. Guests meet at the confirmed ghat; hotel transfers and a flute musician are additional.</p>
<p>A guided river experience gives you time to understand the waterfront as well as photograph it. Your guide can explain the ghats, the morning activities and the relationship between the river and the neighbourhoods above it.</p>
<p>Boarding arrangements, the route and operating times depend on river conditions and local permissions. We confirm these for your travel date.</p>
<h2>Varanasi walking tours: choose the neighbourhood that interests you</h2>
<p>A <strong>Varanasi walking tour</strong> is a good choice for travellers who enjoy exploring at street level. Our guided walks start from <strong>₹1,500 per person</strong>, with a minimum of two guests.</p>
<p>The <a href="/tours/varanasi-walking-tour/">Old City &amp; Northern Bazaar Walk</a> suits visitors interested in busy lanes, neighbourhood shrines and everyday trading activity. Bengali Tola offers another perspective through its riverside lanes, while the Southern Kashi Walk focuses on the Assi area, temples and sacred ponds.</p>
<p>The Death &amp; Rebirth Walk explores beliefs surrounding life, death and ritual. It is conducted with respect for residents, worshippers and bereaved families. Photography restrictions and local customs must be observed.</p>
<p>Most walks begin at an agreed meeting point. Hotel transfers and paid admissions are additional unless included in your quotation. Please tell us about walking difficulties before booking so that we can suggest a suitable route.</p>
<h2>Varanasi food tour price: what is included?</h2>
<p>Our <a href="/experiences/varanasi-food-walk/">Varanasi food walk</a> starts from <strong>₹2,750 per person</strong>, including a specialist culinary guide and selected vegetarian tastings.</p>
<p>The experience introduces Banarasi food through the places and people who prepare it. Depending on the route, season and opening hours, the tasting plan can explore breakfast traditions, savoury snacks, sweets and local drinks.</p>
<p>We confirm the tasting list before the walk. Please share allergies and dietary requirements in advance so that we can assess suitable arrangements. Hotel transfers are additional.</p>
<p>For travellers who prefer a more relaxed experience around a meal, our <a href="/experiences/banarasi-home-cooking/">Banarasi home cooking experience</a> starts from <strong>₹4,500 per person</strong>. It includes a hosted vegetarian cooking session and meal, with the menu and duration agreed beforehand.</p>
