<h2>Cultural experiences beyond the main sightseeing route</h2>
<p>A weaving visit, cooking session or musical performance can add depth to a Varanasi holiday.</p>
<p>The <a href="/experiences/banarasi-silk-weaving/">Banarasi silk and weaving experience</a>, from <strong>₹1,750 per person</strong>, includes a private guide and handloom visit. The <a href="/experiences/banaras-artisan-trail/">Banaras Artisan Trail</a>, from <strong>₹2,250 per person</strong>, offers arranged visits to working artisans. Access depends on the hosts and workshops available for your date; purchases are additional.</p>
<p>A <a href="/experiences/classical-music-varanasi/">private classical music experience</a> or <a href="/experiences/private-kathak-experience/">private Kathak performance</a> starts from <strong>₹13,500 per session</strong>. These arrangements are tailored to the available artists, venue, group size and agreed format. A participatory workshop should be requested separately rather than assumed to form part of a performance.</p>
<h2>How to combine experiences during your stay</h2>
<p>For a first visit, we suggest choosing one principal experience for each part of the day and leaving time for meals, rest and local movement.</p>
<p>A sunrise boat ride can be followed by breakfast and a short walk. Another afternoon can be reserved for Sarnath, with Ganga Aarti arranged on an evening that suits your arrival and sightseeing schedule.</p>
<p>Travellers interested in local culture might combine a weaving visit with a food walk, or choose a cooking session and a private performance on different days.</p>
<p>When several experiences are booked together, ask us for a combined quotation. We can coordinate guide hours and transfers around the complete programme.</p>
